# examples/games/01_pong, played: two whole games, lost and won.
#
# Blue (left) is player one, on W and S; Red (right) is player two, on the
# arrows. Every serve goes towards whoever conceded, starting with Red, along
# (1, 0.35): a paddle left where it is misses it, and a point takes 75 frames.
# See tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar and tools/examples_build.sh for how
# it runs.

# --- the failure path: Red wins 7-0 ------------------------------------------

# Red goes down to meet the first serve. The arrows are Red's ALONE: they
# moved both paddles until this script saw it (examples/games/01_pong).
1 press KEY_DOWN
19 release KEY_DOWN
19 shot arrows_move_red_only

# Red returns it, and Blue goes up and away from it.
100 press KEY_W
110 release KEY_W
200 shot red_scores
200 expect scene PongScene

# Six more serves at Blue, who stays where the serve puts the paddles. The
# seventh point pushes the end of the game on top of the court.
639 expect scene PongScene
640 expect scene OverScene
641 shot red_wins

# The court below is frozen and deaf: Red's keys move nothing now.
645 press KEY_UP
655 release KEY_UP
658 shot court_frozen

# Play again, with the mouse: down on 660, up on 661, the new game from 662.
660 click 400 245
660 expect scene OverScene
661 expect scene PongScene

# --- the happy path: Blue wins 7-0 -------------------------------------------

# Red returns the first serve again, the same way...
663 press KEY_DOWN
681 release KEY_DOWN
# ...and this time Blue goes down to meet it and sends it back,
762 press KEY_S
769 release KEY_S
850 shot blue_returns
# and Red goes up, the wrong way.
900 press KEY_UP
915 release KEY_UP
962 shot blue_scores

# Six serves at Red, who stays put: Blue wins.
1407 expect scene PongScene
1408 expect scene OverScene
1409 shot blue_wins

# Play again, from the keyboard: the button has the focus.
1430 tap KEY_ENTER
1430 expect scene PongScene
1432 shot again
1432 end
